node_modules
dist
build
*.tsbuildinfo
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local
# Recursive so nested secret files (e.g. docker/.env) are excluded from every
# build context, not just the repo root. Keep the committed .env.example.
**/.env
**/.env.*
!.env.example
!**/.env.example
.git
.vscode
.idea
coverage
test-results
playwright-report
*.log
logs
tmp
temp
.claude
# #1115: the repo's Python tools (today `tools/eval-corpus-images/`; the VL
# embedding shim until #1618 stage 2 removed it) put a multi-GB venv inside the
# checkout when you follow their README. docker-compose.build.yml builds with
# `context: ..`, so without these the wheels are tarred up and streamed to the
# daemon on every local source build. Broader than .gitignore's `tools/**`
# equivalents on purpose: this is a build-context filter, not a tracking rule.
**/.venv
**/__pycache__
**/.pytest_cache
**/*.egg-info
